<concept importance="optional" id="t00218">
	<title id="e01353">Forward and backward adjustment </title>
	<shortdesc/>
	<conbody>
		<table colsep="1" frame="none" outputclass="formatc_none" rowsep="1" id="e01354">
			<tgroup cols="2" colsep="0" rowsep="1">
				<colspec colname="col1" colnum="1" colsep="0" colwidth="50*"/>
				<colspec colname="col2" colnum="2" colsep="0" colwidth="50*"/>
				<tbody>
					<row rowsep="1">
						<entry colname="col1">
							<fig id="e01355">
								<image href="images/N_SP327_B06_025.jpg" scale="95" align="center" placement="break"/>
							</fig>
						</entry>
						<entry colname="col2"/>
					</row>
				</tbody>
			</tgroup>
		</table>
		<p>Adjust the headrest by pulling it forward to 1 of 3 different positions.</p>
		<p>To adjust the headrest as far back as it will go, pull it all the way forward and release it.</p>
		<p>Adjust the headrest so that it properly supports the head and neck.</p>
	</conbody>
